if you want to be productive as an  entrepreneur then you need to make sure  you're freeing up your time to focus on  the highest priority tasks otherwise  you're going to be constantly dragged  down and sucked into the day-to-day crap  that's involved in running the business  hi i'm evan carmichael i believe that  hunger entrepreneurs deserve help and  today i'm answering an email from a  question i mention a question from an  email that came in from one of my  readers shahed who wrote a long email  here basically summing it up he has a  cleaning business he's watched a lot of  videos and channels he subscribed to  mine he thanks me a lot thank you for  subscribing anybody watching you can  subscribe too i love seeing that  right now he's losing focus he says he  gets distracted he's by minor  disturbances it takes a lot of time to  get back into gear  uh he's living off of energy boosters  barely gets to the gym  and he's not living a healthy lifestyle  wants to be able to get more stuff done  and wanted my advice  so thanks for the questions i had hey  you know what welcome to the club this  is the life as an entrepreneur right  we're all doing way too much  we're working crazy hours  and the reality is you shouldn't be  doing 80 percent of the things that you  are doing  the way to overcome it  is one eliminate  there's probably things in your business  that you don't need to do and nobody  else should be doing  take it away a quick example  i used to host meetings or i still do  their mastermind meetings we meet once a  month i used to write minutes of what  everybody talked about  and sent off the notes to everybody one  month i forgot you know what happened  nobody cared  at first i felt a little sad you know i  spent all this time every month making  these notes sending them people think  i'm offering a value-added service  and nobody cared  so i stopped doing it and we all have  those things in our businesses i still  look for them now today in mind  things that you're doing that you should  just not do they are not adding enough  value to your business you need to  eliminate them  second you need to automate  find software tools systems that you can  use  to  get a lot of things off your plate if  i'm doing something repetitively if i do  it two or three times i find a way to  make it automatic  i'll have my programmer create a tool or  i'll find something off the shelf i use  a web tool some software whatever i can  find to automate things  because computers don't take  vacations they don't call in sick and  they take a lot of the crap off of your  plate and off of your team  and the third is delegate  you need  to get rid of the rest of those tasks  give them off to somebody who can do it  maybe even better than you but basically  you're trying to free up your time to  focus on the high priority projects if  you're stuck doing all the crap all the  time on your business you're never going  to get anywhere you're going to you're  going to level off here you're never  going to be able to get  way higher  because your time is spent doing the  tasks that you should not be doing you  need to build a team  you need to offload those tasks  that have to get done in the business  that can't be eliminated that can't be  automated through software or other  tools that still need some personal  connection to do it but it doesn't have  to be you and the last bit of device i  have is chunk your time  this has been so helpful for me  where anything that you do multiple  times a day do once a day  if you're checking your email 20 times a  day do it once a day anything you do  multiple times a week is once a week  multiple times a month once a month and  so on  it gets you in the zone i find that when  i'm switching gears  you know if i'm working on something and  somebody calls me  i help you know whatever answer the  question is then i get back to work i've  lost what i was doing you know takes me  20 30 minutes to get back into the flow  of what i was doing so i don't list my  phone number anymore  nobody calls me nobody knows my number  it's not on my website it's not on my  business card i don't even know the  number to my cell phone i needed it once  and i had to write to my dad to say  what's my cell phone number  phone calls incoming unscheduled phone  calls are other people's agenda for your  time you need to protect your time it's  the most important thing you have in  your business  i'll chunk things up in the days  so for example i'm doing these videos  i'm answering your question i love doing  videos i always do videos on a wednesday  i block off the afternoon to do videos  on a wednesday  i love it it's one of the best times i  have in the day but it takes setup time  you know i gotta set up the cameras  microphone but more i have to get in the  zone  i have to think about helping people  you know the first video is not always  the best it takes me a while to get into  it it takes me a while to get out of it  so it's better to chunk it all together  if i said i'm going to do one video a  day it would take me a lot longer to do  each day because there's so much setup  physically with equipment more mentally  where if i do one after another after  another for another it's easier to get  in that flow  i'll do my meetings on thursdays  anything where i'm interacting with  people it's on thursdays my radio shows  on thursdays my webinars are on  thursdays my mastermind meetings are on  thursdays if i have phone calls or  meetings they're on thursdays  that's my meeting day that's my talk to  the people get stuff done day  because i found  when i'm getting ready for a phone call  or a meeting  the first you know half an hour into it  before the meeting nothing gets done  if i know i'm going to meet somebody in  half an hour 20 minutes  it's hard to get into a project  right you fiddle around you do little  things but nothing major  because you know it has to end in 20 30  minutes  so i put the meetings back to back to  back to back to back and thursday is  full of meetings  and phone calls and the webinars and all  that stuff so i'm not wasting my time  then the very next day fridays i'll do  my worksheets it's my writing day i want  to come to the office you should go to  starbucks  and i'll sit down and i'll write the  whole day i don't take any phone calls  they don't answer email i just sit and  write  because when i'm writing i need to get  into zone two  and i don't want to get distracted  one email one phone call can set me off  and then i forget where i was and i've  lost my train of focus  so chunk up your day and be ferocious  about guarding your time don't let  people  waste your time  force them onto your schedule  and lastly you need to build up ceo time  you need to have a part of your day  every day that you spend on things that  are growing your business  not the tasks that you do in your  business growth new opportunities new  projects hiring people raising capital  whatever it is new things that are going  to grow your business you need to make  sure you have that time that has to be  built in and you have to safeguard it  and protect it  because if you don't have new  opportunities coming into your business  you're always going to be stuck where  you are  you're never going to be able to grow  and get to that next step i'll work on a  new project build it up to a certain  point decide if i'm going to keep it or  lose it  if i'm keeping it i give it to somebody  to manage and i'm on to my next project  if i lose it i lose it try something new  you have to make sure you have your ceo  time a lot of information in one video  it got me riled up but a very important  topic because most entrepreneurs suck at  time management and people chew their  time and you can't afford to have your  time wasted  at least i can't  you shouldn't either  don't accept people walking all over you  you have to set up the barriers  thank you guys for watching you like  this video please give it a thumbs up  below and i want to hear from you please  leave a comment with your thoughts under  this video or if you have a question for  your own business i'd love to hear it in  the comments i always read those i  really do appreciate them and i love  seeing them come in so thank you guys  and i'll see you soon

